From 459e055a7a9d8ad718a5ff103df8acc6b3746fc0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AERA | Erez Yaary <yaary@me.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 10:15:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] common/ui/badge.c: the family's boxed badge in the 6 x 6 font

From EPlay's bar (0.27: "320 KBPS", "44.1 KHZ", "DSP"), so every app's
badges look alike, the Hebrew keyboard's badge among them (the hub,
5 Nov 2026).

A badge is made once, as its text changes, into a one-plane form from
the Line-A font's own glyphs, and now its box too, so it is drawn with
one transparent raster copy (EPlay's drew the box as four filled
rectangles beside it). Where the font isn't TOS's the box is in the form
still and the text is the VDI's, and badge_vdi says so, for an app that
keeps the VDI's attributes in step. A text over 21 characters, or a cell
over 8 rows, is drawn the VDI's way whole.

tests/badge: test_badge.c checks the form on the build machine (box,
glyphs in place, the clear pixel round the text, the limits, no font,
another height), with AddressSanitizer: all pass. BADGECMP.PRG draws
each badge with badge_draw and the VDI's way (four rectangles, the 6 x 6
text transparent) on plain and patterned grounds, in every pen up to 16,
on and off a 16-pixel group, in rows of 10 to 24, after a text change
and clipped at each edge, and compares the two byte for byte, on EmuTOS:

  Falcon:16     251 badges, 0 differ; 550 us a badge, the VDI's 2,450
  Falcon-4:16   251 badges, 0 differ; 750 us, the VDI's 4,950
  ST:mono        27 badges, 0 differ; 2,100 us, the VDI's 10,650
  ST:med         59 badges, 0 differ; 2,650 us, the VDI's 12,700

AESGAP: no app draws with it yet. EPlay takes it on its next sync, and
its rows' figures come with that change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SZeNoDozTmbWt4s2sFN9eL
